{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162282-what-spheres-would-these-types-of-characters-need","id":1162282,"title":"What spheres would these types of characters need?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-24T16:43:56-08:00","id":1162282,"title":"What spheres would these types of characters need?","content":"A witch that uses tarot cards, does mental stuff, and has a wide variety of spells. What would you think (besides the Mind sphere) they'd need?<br /> <br /> And secondly, religion-based characters such as a priest, a firebrand pastor or a female church singer. What would they realistically be able to do if we are operating within the parameters of their genre?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T16:58:15-08:00","id":1162285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162282-what-spheres-would-these-types-of-characters-need#post1162282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A witch that uses tarot cards, does mental stuff, and has a wide variety of spells. What would you think (besides the Mind sphere) they'd need?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Tarot is usually for divination, so Time 2, maybe Correspondence 2 and/or Entropy 1. Mind 2 to influence people's minds while doing a reading IIRC. Beyond that, using the Major Arcana or the face cards of the suites to summon associated spirits (Spirit 2) or physical attacks (Forces 2/Life 2). Using readings as a focus for healing or influence a person's fortune (Life 2/Entropy 2). That's just off the top of my head. Someone else may have more detailed ideas. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T17:14:08-08:00","id":1162288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162282-what-spheres-would-these-types-of-characters-need?p=1162285#post1162285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Tarot is usually for divination, so Time 2, maybe Correspondence 2 and/or Entropy 1. Mind 2 to influence people's minds while doing a reading IIRC. Beyond that, using the Major Arcana or the face cards of the suites to summon associated spirits (Spirit 2) or physical attacks (Forces 2/Life 2). Using readings as a focus for healing or influence a person's fortune (Life 2/Entropy 2). That's just off the top of my head. Someone else may have more detailed ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>What can be done with forces 2 and life 2? I thought you needed forces 3 and prime 2 to conjure fire, and life 3 to inflict pattern damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T20:13:43-08:00","id":1162332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162282-what-spheres-would-these-types-of-characters-need?p=1162288#post1162288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What can be done with forces 2 and life 2? I thought you needed forces 3 and prime 2 to conjure fire, and life 3 to inflict pattern damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Life 2 you can get a nearby tree to grab or swipe at someone or cause insects to swarm. With Forces 2 you can paralyze someone by dynamically draining off their kinetic energy; normally the spontaneity of the body would make the success threshold pretty high there, but it is less so with the addition of Life 2.<br /> <br /> I would consider doing as much or more Entropy as Mind. Manipulating fate and fortune is classic witchery, especially when you're using fortune-associated foci like Tarot cards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T20:42:54-08:00","id":1162334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162282-what-spheres-would-these-types-of-characters-need#post1162282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And secondly, religion-based characters such as a priest, a firebrand pastor or a female church singer. What would they realistically be able to do if we are operating within the parameters of their genre?</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be a good place to start: <a href=\"http://www.miraclesofthesaints.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.miraclesofthesaints.com</a> (Since Catholicism is a widespread modern religion I should mention I am neither endorsing nor belittling this website. It was just one of the first Google results I came across). From these examples it seems like a lot is possible, you just have to make sure the Foci are consistent with the paradigm. Add in some of the Jesus stuff and you have examples from every single Sphere. You can achieve a lot of Mind Effects Coincidentally just through charismatic preaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T23:09:25-08:00","id":1162369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162282-what-spheres-would-these-types-of-characters-need#post1162282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And secondly, religion-based characters such as a priest, a firebrand pastor or a female church singer. What would they realistically be able to do if we are operating within the parameters of their genre?</div> </div> </div> </div>The White Wolf Wiki's list of abilities associated with True Faith is also a reasonable start of abilities that could be paradigmatically emulated: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/True_Faith\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/True_Faith</a> This isn't to say your character has access to True Faith, just that it has a reasonable list of religiously associated powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T02:48:30-08:00","id":1162405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1162282-what-spheres-would-these-types-of-characters-need#post1162282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A witch that uses tarot cards, does mental stuff, and has a wide variety of spells. What would you think (besides the Mind sphere) they'd need?</div> </div> </div> </div>Time and Entropy could be considered in regards to using a deck of Tarot cards as a Foci for divinations (Time 2 and Entropy 1). Individual Tarot cards could also be used as Foci for Correspondence Spells and Rotes (Correspondence Sense, Correspondence 2 and 3 scrying). Herbalism (brewing various potions and mixtures) could be a Foci for Life and Mind 1 Spells and Rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T06:08:14-08:00","id":1162445,"title":"","content":"Here's another question: what are these two characters' political affiliations? What groups, if any, do they belong to?<br /> <br /> Depending on the answer, it could mandate certain Spheres, on account of how groups have their particular Specialty Spheres. M20 allows more flexibility in this regard than previous editions (which had only one Sphere to choose per sect), but it's still a choice between a certain number of them. If the witch is a Verbana, they HAVE to take either Life or Forces for one Sphere dot. A Hollow One or independent witch, though, could choose any Specialty Sphere they wanted. Same with the religious character, which could be a Chorister, Templar, a different group, or none at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}